      "loudness": "Loud",
      "description": "A gushing burst of sweet, clear, shrill and emphatic music: a few preliminary notes run into a slightly ascending trill and end in full clear notes or another trill; remarkably loud for the bird's size. Given from an exposed low perch, the male's whole body quivering with effort, most often in spring but audible year-round.",
